OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AChris Mason: Will Burnham find PMQs as
OL,4,A'nail biting' and 'nerve wracking' as
OL,5,ABlair did?
OL,6,
OL,7,FSir Tony Blair wrote that "PMQs was the
OL,8,Fmost nerve wracking, discombobulating,
OL,9,Fnail biting, bowel moving, terror
OL,10,Finspiring, courage draining experience
OL,11,Fin my prime ministerial life, without
OL,12,Fquestion".
OL,14,FNow, for the first time, it is Andy
OL,15,FBurnham's turn to feel those nerves.
OL,16,FAnd yet, curiously, the questions at
OL,17,Flunchtime may well feel like a minor
OL,18,Fextension to the three and a half hours
OL,19,Fof questions he faced on Tuesday
OL,20,Fafternoon.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/39
